  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday) Issued at 115 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nSlightly cooler temperatures are forecast on Tuesday behind the \nfront, with highs near seasonal normals. Expect highs in the low to \nmid 70s for most locations. Overnight lows will be in the mid 40s to \nnear 50. Near seasonal temperatures and dry conditions are forecast \nWednesday through Friday. Another weak cold front will track south \nacross the forecast area late Thursday into Friday morning. Highs \nthese days will be in the 70s, with overnight lows mainly in the mid \n40s to lower 50s. \n\nModels begin to diverge with respect to the synoptic pattern next \nweekend. The GFS tracks a weak trough across the Southern Plains, \nwhile the ECMWF indicates a much more potent trough and develops an \nupper level low across northeast Mexico on Saturday. The ECMWF would \nresult in a wetter solution, while the GFS would result in a much \ndrier forecast. For now, PoPs were kept in the low to medium \ncategory (20-30%), but these will likely need to be adjusted in the \ncoming days.",
